            Garden of Life Raw Organic Meal looks like the bargain, and per serving it is. But it delivers 150 calories, so if you add a banana and a spoon of nut butter to make it a real meal, the true cost per meal rises and the calorie count closes in on the others. Always compare cost per meal that you would actually drink, not cost per scoop.
          </p>

          <p>
            If one number matters most to you, use it to break ties. For satiety, choose on calories and fiber. For muscle and appetite control, choose on protein per serving. For a budget, choose on cost per meal including any add-ins. For convenience, a bottle beats a bag every time, at a price. Our full <a href="/protein-powder-comparison/">protein powder comparison</a> uses the same method for plain protein tubs.
